,"type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"): sweeps in vertex index order, each vertex not holding a most-voted","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"label taking the greatest of them, until a sweep changes nothing. Deterministic; on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symmetric graphs (a ring of cliques) one label can flood the graph, which the ","type":"text"},{"code":"using:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" form","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"usually avoids.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/communitydetection\/graphprotocols\/graph\/asynchronouslabelpropagationcommunities()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"asynchronousLabelPropagationCommunities","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Partition","preciseIdentifier":"s:18CommunityDetection9PartitionV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedView","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols12DirectedViewV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">>","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/CommunityDetection\/documentation\/CommunityDetection\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/asynchronousLabelPropagationCommunities()","type":"topic","title":"asynchronousLabelPropagationCommunities()"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph","title":"Graph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between them. Kept apart from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":": an undirected graph is not a symmetric directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "